{"requirements":[{"id":"prevent-loading-now","requirement":"Prevent the usb-storage kernel module from loading on node1 in the current boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The module was initially unloaded. After the deny policy was installed, an explicit modprobe attempt failed with the install rule `/bin/false`, and usb_storage remained unloaded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb11343bbe694e6b","cmd-c3fab1ac008d4b64","cmd-e45687c126ad442d"]},{"id":"prevent-loading-after-reboot","requirement":"Ensure usb-storage remains blocked after node1 reboots.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded reboot was observed: node1 began healthy, acknowledged the scheduled reboot, changed boot ID, and recovered to a running state with a read-write root filesystem. Afterward, the persistent policy remained present, an explicit load attempt failed, usb_storage was not loaded, and the rebuilt initramfs omitted the module. Fixed lifecycle observations independently confirm the boot-ID change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fb11343bbe694e6b","cmd-7fbb60652c3c4151","cmd-fa4875b5a66346d4","cmd-09ac81dc63ec4f3c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"The required configuration, final initramfs rebuild, verification, and reboot were appropriately scoped. One unnecessary mutation occurred: the first initramfs rebuild did not embed the policy or omit the module and was superseded by the later successful rebuild, so it was effectively reverted/overwritten. Two evidence probes also left `/tmp/usb-storage-load.out` and `/tmp/usb-storage-postboot.out` behind rather than cleaning them up. No failed services, new network exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-50d2fa7bb0b944f6","cmd-1afa8f29175a4ce8","cmd-c981cb6029684224","cmd-c3fab1ac008d4b64","cmd-09ac81dc63ec4f3c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied with direct pre- and post-reboot behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is coherent for the single managed node and is independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities. Minor hygiene deductions apply for a superseded initramfs rebuild and two retained scratch files.","limitations":[]}
